.el .ds Aq '
.TH whittle 1  "whittle 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
whittle \- Tag\-aware long\-read trimmer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwhittle\fR [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-out\-format\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-min\-length\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-max\-length\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-min\-qual\fR] [\fB\-Q\fR|\fB\-\-max\-qual\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-min\-gc\fR] [\fB\-G\fR|\fB\-\-max\-gc\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-qual\-mode\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-head\-crop\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-tail\-crop\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-trim\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-best\-segment\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-split\fR] [\fB\-\-qual\-split\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-moves\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\-policy\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tag\-aware long\-read trimmer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SETUP
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Input FASTQ\-family file, unaligned BAM, or directory. Reads stdin when omitted
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output file. Writes stdout when omitted; the path extension selects its format
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-format\fR \fI<IN_FORMAT>\fR
Force the input format instead of detecting it from the path or stream
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz
.IP \(bu 2
bam
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-format\fR \fI<OUT_FORMAT>\fR
Force the output format instead of selecting it from the output path
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz
.IP \(bu 2
bam
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads (default: all detected CPUs; values above the CPU count are clamped)
.TP
\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR \fI<FASTQ_TAGS>\fR [default: all]
BAM auxiliary tags copied into BAM\-to\-FASTQ headers: all, none, or a list such as MM,ML,RG
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-compression\-level\fR \fI<COMPRESSION_LEVEL>\fR
DEFLATE compression level for compressed output (bgzf for BAM, gzip for FASTQ.gz). Lower = faster/larger. Ignored for plain FASTQ. Default when unset: 4 for gzip FASTQ output, 6 for BGZF (BAM and .bgz)
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write a machine\-readable JSON run summary (counters plus the resolved settings) to this path. Written even under \-\-quiet
.SH LOGGING
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase logging detail: \-v = debug, \-vv = trace (maximum two). Overridden by WHITTLE_LOG
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Silence progress and info output; warnings and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How to report progress, independently of the log level: a bar on a terminal and periodic lines otherwise (auto), always one or the other, or none at all while keeping the banner and summary
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, periodic lines otherwise
.IP \(bu 2
bar: Always the animated bar
.IP \(bu 2
plain: Always periodic lines, never a bar
.IP \(bu 2
none: No progress reporting; the banner and summary still print
.RE
.SH FILTERING
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-min\-length\fR \fI<MIN_LENGTH>\fR [default: 1]
Minimum post\-trim segment length
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-max\-length\fR \fI<MAX_LENGTH>\fR
Maximum post\-trim segment length
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-min\-qual\fR \fI<MIN_QUAL>\fR [default: 0]
Minimum post\-trim read quality under \-\-qual\-mode
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-max\-qual\fR \fI<MAX_QUAL>\fR [default: 1000]
Maximum post\-trim read quality under \-\-qual\-mode
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-min\-gc\fR \fI<MIN_GC>\fR
Minimum post\-trim GC fraction (0\-1)
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-max\-gc\fR \fI<MAX_GC>\fR
Maximum post\-trim GC fraction (0\-1)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-qual\-mode\fR \fI<QUAL_MODE>\fR [default: mean]
Read\-quality summary used by the quality filters
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mean: Average error probabilities, then convert the result back to Phred Q
.IP \(bu 2
arithmetic: Take the arithmetic mean of the per\-base Phred scores
.IP \(bu 2
median: Take the median per\-base Phred score
.RE
.SH TRIMMING
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-head\-crop\fR \fI<HEAD_CROP>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from the 5\*(Aq end before other trimming
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-tail\-crop\fR \fI<TAIL_CROP>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from the 3\*(Aq end before other trimming
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-trim\fR \fI<QUAL_TRIM>\fR
Trim low\-quality bases from both ends until each boundary reaches Q
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-best\-segment\fR \fI<QUAL_BEST_SEGMENT>\fR
Keep the longest contiguous segment whose bases are all at least Q
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-split\fR \fI<QUAL_SPLIT>\fR
Split at low\-quality runs below Q and keep the surviving segments
.TP
\fB\-\-qual\-split\-window\fR \fI<QUAL_SPLIT_WINDOW>\fR [default: 1]
Tolerate low\-quality runs shorter than this many bases when splitting
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-moves\fR
Keep ONT signal tags consistent through trimming (slice `mv`, update `ts`/`ns`/`sp`/`pi`) for signal\-aware tools (Remora, Clair3 v2), instead of dropping them. BAM→BAM only
.SH "ADAPTER TRIMMING"
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR \fI<ADAPTER_FASTA>\fR
Adapter FASTA (each sequence >= the 11\-bp minimum match length). Enables adapter trimming
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR \fI<ADAPTER_PRESET>\fR [default: none]
Built\-in ONT adapter catalog. Enables adapter trimming
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
none: Do not load a built\-in adapter catalog
.IP \(bu 2
ont: Load the built\-in Oxford Nanopore adapter and barcode catalog
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR \fI<ADAPTER_ERROR_RATE>\fR [default: 0.2]
End\-match tolerance (fraction of adapter length). Interior splits use half
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-size\fR \fI<ADAPTER_END_SIZE>\fR [default: 150]
Bases at each read end searched for a terminal adapter
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR
Trim adapters at read ends only; never split on interior adapters
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\fR \fI<ADAPTER_SAMPLE>\fR
Reads sampled for preset detection or ab\-initio inference. Defaults to 0 for preset detection and 40000 for inference; inference requires >=100
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\fR [\fI<ADAPTER_INFER>\fR]
Discover adapters de novo. With no value, defaults to trim; report prints inferred FASTA and exits without writing read output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
trim: Trim reads with the inferred sequences
.IP \(bu 2
report: Print inferred FASTA to stdout and do not write read output
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-infer\-policy\fR \fI<ADAPTER_INFER_POLICY>\fR
Trust policy for inferred consensuses (default: conservative). Aggressive uses the complete consensus and permits splitting unless ends\-only is set
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
conservative: Use a short end\-facing anchor and disable inferred interior splitting
.IP \(bu 2
aggressive: Use the complete recurrent consensus and allow interior splitting
.RE
